From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] Record each queue's device, so latches and completion watches
 find it

cabooseGetQueueDevice read info_VkQueue, whose device nothing ever set, so it
always returned VK_NULL_HANDLE: no media latch was ever written (a phone-decoded
picture never reached the image that samples it), and every completion watch
was keyed to device 0.

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
index c873eb9..8601ef9 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
@@ -7299,6 +7299,9 @@ VkResult ResourceTracker::cabooseExportSyncFile(void* context, VkDevice device,
 void ResourceTracker::cabooseNoteQueue(VkDevice device, VkQueue queue, uint32_t family) {
     std::lock_guard<std::recursive_mutex> lock(mLock);
     mCabooseDeviceQueues.emplace(device, std::make_pair(queue, family));
+    // The queue's device, for what a submission names by queue alone (media latches,
+    // completion watches): nothing else records it.
+    info_VkQueue[queue].device = device;
 }
 
 // Tells the broker which image holds the buffer's pixels, so the compositor can show it.
